Dialogue: 0,0:39:42.40,0:39:48.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,that um this perspective is also saying that uh we need a robot the like\N也就是说，我们还需要一个机器人，就像这样
Dialogue: 0,0:39:48.64,0:39:55.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,more subtle view of this is that ro we need a lot of these primitive\N更微妙的看法是，我们需要大量这些基础组件
Dialogue: 0,0:39:55.36,0:39:59.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,actions to present in the v like in the pre-trained vas because as you can\N在视觉模型中呈现动作，就像在预训练的视觉模型中一样，因为如你所见
Dialogue: 0,0:39:59.80,0:40:05.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you can imagine that a lot of these uh diverse pre-training robot data is\N如果你能想象，这些多样化的预训练机器人数据
Dialogue: 0,0:40:05.52,0:40:09.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,giving the policy the ability to actually do these kind of little primitives attach like\N赋予政策执行这类微小基础操作的能力
Dialogue: 0,0:40:09.93,0:40:13.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,picking up nails and putting nails in the in in the in the toolbox and everything.\N捡起钉子，把钉子放进工具箱里，一切就绪。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:13.80,0:40:19.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,What a human data essentially does is to string these behaviors together to solve a long task.\N人类数据本质上是将这些行为串联起来，以完成一项长期任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:19.12,0:40:23.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we don't actually need a lot of human data to make these work.\N所以我们实际上不需要大量人类数据就能让它们运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:23.07,0:40:31.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, so this this kind of brings to actually to two two two perspective of human to robot transfer that happens only at scale.\N所以，这实际上带来了两种人类到机器人迁移的视角，而这只有在规模化时才会发生。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:31.84,0:40:41.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first perspective is more straightforward is that if you have a lot of human data, if you post train robot data with some align aligned data,\N第一种观点更直接：如果你有大量的人类数据，就可以用一些对齐过的数据对机器人数据进行后训练。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:41.20,0:40:48.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh align human data, robot data and humanlike robots really enable strong human to robot transfer at scale, right?\N啊，对齐人类数据、机器人数据和类人机器人，确实能大规模实现高效的人机迁移，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:40:48.32,0:40:50.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is just pre-training post- training story.\N这只是一个预训练和后训练的故事。
Dialogue: 0,0:40:50.56,0:40:56.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but what the π collaboration is saying is that maybe the foundation\N但 π 合作项目所说的是，也许基础……
Dialogue: 0,0:40:56.30,0:41:01.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,is not human data is a lot of diverse embodiment that supports the transfer from\N并非人类数据，而是大量多样的具身形态，支持了迁移。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:01.60,0:41:08.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,like more diverse human behavior to to different robots right so it's really diverse diverse\N比如让机器人表现出更多样化的类人行为，所以它真的非常多样化。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:08.80,0:41:15.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,embodiment data allows human to transfer uh human to transfer a human robot transfer to emerge\N具身数据使人类能够实现人机迁移，从而让机器人具备人类能力
Dialogue: 0,0:41:15.35,0:41:20.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,and I'm not suggesting if either of this is will be the final picture I'm\N我并不是说这两种情况中的任何一种会是最终的图景
Dialogue: 0,0:41:20.05,0:41:25.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,just saying that at scale uh different things would emerge that don't emer that don't\N只是说，规模达到一定程度后，会出现一些原本不会出现的新情况。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:25.67,0:41:32.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,happen when you work on small scale problems and uh depending on what hypothesis you\N当你处理小规模问题时，会遇到各种情况，这取决于你所采用的假设。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:32.72,0:41:38.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,have uh for like how you view human robot transfer problem you might find different things.\N嗯，就像你看待人机迁移问题的方式不同，可能会发现不同的东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:38.31,0:41:49.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,So there's not a single uh like answer to this human robot transfer problem and there's it's a vast space of exploration to be done in this space.\N因此，人机迁移问题并没有单一的答案，这个领域还有广阔的空间等待探索。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:49.61,0:41:50.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:41:50.64,0:41:58.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So on that note, uh I think it's it's it's time to answer the question that if a lot of things happen at scale,\N那么说到这儿，我觉得是时候回答这个问题了：如果大量事情都在规模化发生，
Dialogue: 0,0:41:58.28,0:42:01.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh if academia, what's the real academia, right?\N呃，如果说到学术界，真正的学术界，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:42:01.39,0:42:09.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like how can we actually drive drive the science of this like is just a big company or like the fancy frontier lab problem now, right?\N我们到底该如何真正推动这一科学的发展？现在难道不就是一家大公司或一个高端前沿实验室的问题吗？
Dialogue: 0,0:42:09.97,0:42:19.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, so the final question I want to kind of hint at is maybe there's a way for us to also scale the scientific understanding of human robot transfer.\N所以，我想暗示的最后一个问题可能是，我们是否也能在人类与机器人迁移的科学理解上实现扩展。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:19.56,0:42:28.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so um so because because I mean the making scientific progress is not really like a company thing is it's it's a collective community thing.\N嗯，所以说，科学进步其实并不像公司那样运作，对吧？它是一个集体社区共同参与的事。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:28.61,0:42:36.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,If we look at the history of AI, many of the major breakthroughs were enabled by community-scale infrastructure, like ImageNet and MS COCO.\N如果我们回顾人工智能的发展史，许多重大突破都是由社区规模的基础设施推动的，\N比如 ImageNet 和 MS COCO。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:36.82,0:42:41.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,enabled the the blossom of a lot of the deep learning ar uh\N推动了深度学习的蓬勃发展
Dialogue: 0,0:42:41.50,0:42:46.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,deep deep learning techniques and computer vision advancements and detection seation and all\N深度学习技术、计算机视觉进步、检测定位以及所有相关领域
Dialogue: 0,0:42:46.33,0:42:57.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,those kind of things and uh common crawl sorry games enabled advances in reinforced learning for a while and super glue uh really test stress tested\N这类东西，还有 Common Crawl——抱歉，游戏曾推动强化学习发展了一段时间，\N而 SuperGLUE 则真正经受了严苛的考验。
Dialogue: 0,0:42:57.20,0:43:07.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,a lot of these language models and common crawl was part of the foundation for a lot of these modern LMS because it's just basically internet.zip,\N许多语言模型和通用爬虫数据构成了现代语言模型的基础，因为它本质上就是互联网的压缩包。
