Dialogue: 0,0:45:03.72,0:45:09.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was a lot of effort to actually pull together a few uh labs and companies to do this kind of things.\N真正把几个实验室和公司凑在一起做这种事，花费了大量精力。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:09.14,0:45:14.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I'm just going to show you like a nice one minute uh promotional video to this.\N但我只是想给你们看一个大约一分钟的宣传视频。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:14.34,0:45:20.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so this is this is a group of labs and companies coming together to study like form attempting\N嗯，这是一群实验室和公司聚集在一起，共同研究类似形态的尝试
Dialogue: 0,0:45:20.88,0:45:26.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,to form a foundation for for studying human robot transfer right so uh Stanford is actually part of it.\N为研究人机迁移奠定基础，因此斯坦福实际上也参与其中。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:26.37,0:45:35.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,So Shiran's lab was a like major collaborator for our efforts and and uh what we kind of I mean the euro story\N因此，施兰实验室是我们项目的重要合作伙伴，我们可以说，这正是欧洲故事的开端。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:35.70,0:45:40.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,we need a lot of data so we collect a lot of I'm going to talk about data set design and all that so\N我们需要大量数据，因此我们会收集大量数据，接下来我将谈谈数据集设计等相关内容。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:40.26,0:45:47.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,but the number of hours is small but it's it's growing right so this is not a fixed data set we actually are continuing\N但小时数虽然不多，却在持续增长，所以这并不是一个固定的数据集，我们实际上仍在持续扩展。
Dialogue: 0,0:45:47.31,0:45:54.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,to pull to pull together data from labs from companies uh to to put together a common data source so it's it's increasing as\N整合来自实验室和公司的数据，建立一个共享的数据源，使其不断增长
Dialogue: 0,0:45:54.51,0:46:03.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,we're speaking Um and we also did cross institute study of a lot of these like basic hypothesis does align data actually matter\N我们正在讨论，此外，我们还对这些基本假设进行了跨机构研究，发现实际数据确实很重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:03.48,0:46:14.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you have different robots right um and it it's it's really an ecosystem for uh for studying this problem uh scientifically at scale\N如果你有不同类型的机器人，这实际上是一个科学地大规模研究这一问题的生态系统。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:14.85,0:46:21.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,and it's made of four parts uh one is data set uh the other is uh platform tools so we have different kind of\N它由四个部分组成，一个是数据集，另一个是平台工具，我们有不同类型
Dialogue: 0,0:46:21.74,0:46:29.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,ways to aggregate your data to allow you anyone in your a this audience who have like maybe an iPhone to collect the data.\N把你的数据聚合起来，这样观众中任何拥有 iPhone 的人，都可以收集数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:29.41,0:46:38.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and we have a research study to really solidify some of the hypothesis we had throughout the the journey of studying this problem and we'll have a\N而且我们有一项研究，旨在真正验证我们在研究这一问题过程中形成的一些假设，我们很快就会公布。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:38.89,0:46:45.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,like consortium made of like labs and uh industry researchers industry startups to to\N一个由实验室和产业研究人员、产业初创公司组成的联盟
Dialogue: 0,0:46:45.57,0:46:51.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,to really come together contributing data insights robots and everything to study this problem.\N真正汇聚起来，贡献数据、洞察、机器人以及一切资源，来研究这个问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:51.65,0:46:58.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,In data set design we did it uh carefully to really uh uh to kind of divide it into two part.\N在数据集设计上，我们谨慎地将其划分为两部分。
Dialogue: 0,0:46:58.67,0:47:04.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,One is what we call a flagship task where we have unified task semantics like folding\N一个是所谓的旗舰任务，我们统一了任务语义，比如蛋白质折叠
Dialogue: 0,0:47:04.64,0:47:09.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,shirts uh uh like classic tasks like cup and saucer which is actually invented by shlab.\N衬衫啊，就像经典的杯子和碟子任务，这其实是由什拉布发明的。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:09.83,0:47:12.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,All of these tasks are standard semantics.\N所有这些任务都是标准语义。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:12.97,0:47:17.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,We uh we had many people across different labs across companies collect\N我们这边，不同实验室、不同公司的很多人参与了收集
Dialogue: 0,0:47:17.24,0:47:20.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,the exact same task on different environment different objects and different everything.\N在不同环境、不同物体以及所有其他条件都不同的情况下执行完全相同的任务。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:20.75,0:47:27.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we have a common foundation for study these tasks and there's also a large pool of free form data like in\N因此我们有了研究这些任务的共同基础，同时也存在大量自由形式的数据，例如
Dialogue: 0,0:47:27.88,0:47:35.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,the wild data that has a longtail distribution behaviors collected by the these companies and then they contributed to the data sets.\N这些公司收集的具有长尾分布特征的海量数据，随后被贡献到数据集中。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:35.12,0:47:45.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that makes up the two parts of the data set and uh like before we really care about turning human data into robot-like data.\N因此，这就构成了数据集的两个部分，就像之前一样，我们真正关心的是如何将人类数据转化为机器人数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:45.28,0:47:54.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we actually added a lot of annotations including these nice uh hand pose, head pose and we also added dense language annotation on top.\N所以我们实际上添加了大量标注，包括这些不错的手部姿态、头部姿态，还增加了密集的语言标注。
Dialogue: 0,0:47:54.08,0:47:58.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so it's very very expensive to do this and I'm really thankful for the who\N呃，做这个非常非常昂贵，我真的很感谢那些人
Dialogue: 0,0:47:58.46,0:48:04.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,the company who actually did all of these annotations on these uh 10400 hours of data.\N实际上对这10400小时数据完成所有标注的公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:04.42,0:48:04.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:04.78,0:48:11.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,But in moving into future all the data will have this kind of uh of data density and in and one\N但当迈向未来时，所有数据都将具有这种数据密度。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:11.90,0:48:17.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,of the most important design decisions for for for eagle verse is that we don't want to just create one data set.\NEgoVerse 最重要的设计决策之一是，我们并不只想创建一个数据集。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:17.58,0:48:23.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,We want it to continue to grow because we don't think a 1400 hour data is going to be enough to capture\N我们希望它能持续增长，因为我们认为1400小时的数据还不够用。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:23.84,0:48:30.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,all of the possible human behaviors everywhere because a large pool of behavior that we don't we haven't done is uh I was\N所有可能的人类行为，因为存在大量我们尚未经历的行为池，这让我感到……
Dialogue: 0,0:48:30.88,0:48:35.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,talking to Mac today is that like we we want we want to study human human interaction right like a lot of these\N今天和麦克斯聊天，就是我们想研究人类之间的互动，就像这些一样
Dialogue: 0,0:48:36.00,0:48:42.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,are still not captured in this data set and we want everything to be uh kind of pulled together to this data source.\N这些数据集尚未涵盖，我们希望所有内容都能汇聚到这一数据源中。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:42.51,0:48:46.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we actually had uh this thing hosted on a cloud flare.\N所以我们实际上把这东西部署在了 Cloudflare 上。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:46.18,0:48:52.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,his R1 instance was right now it's about like 10 terabytes of data but it's still growing uh it's 10 terabytes\N他的 R1 实例目前大约有 10TB 数据，但仍在持续增长，现在是 10TB。
Dialogue: 0,0:48:52.72,0:48:59.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,because we did a lot of compression so that it's manageable uh uh and and we also have a nice like SQL\N因为我们做了大量压缩，使其易于管理，而且我们还拥有一个不错的类似 SQL 的功能
Dialogue: 0,0:48:59.44,0:49:05.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,tables and data exploration web pages on top and so if you're interested you can go explore eagle burst.ai AI there's a\N顶部是表格和数据探索网页，如果你感兴趣，可以去探索一下 egoverse.ai。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:05.76,0:49:14.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,data browser there and uh and we know that not everyone can afford uh this kind of data collection effort at scale.\N数据浏览器在这里，而且我们知道，并不是每个人都能负担得起这种大规模的数据收集工作。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:14.24,0:49:21.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we uh decided to kind of make available an uh in addition to the project Arya glasses uh\N所以我们决定，除了 Arya 眼镜项目之外，再额外提供一些内容。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:21.21,0:49:27.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is the the default device we use in iPhone app that's able to allow you to capture this data.\N这就是我们在 iPhone 应用中默认使用的设备，能够让你捕获这些数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:27.39,0:49:33.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it does uh on the cloud server it does uh data pro postprocessing labeling and everything.\N所以它在云服务器上进行数据的后处理、标注等所有操作。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:33.12,0:49:39.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh so that can you also collect data for yourself for your own research or contribute back to eagors.\N嗯，所以你也可以为自己收集数据，用于自己的研究，或者回馈给EAGORs。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:39.24,0:49:39.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:39.88,0:49:40.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:40.51,0:49:44.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the third part of this is the study.\N第三部分是研究。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:44.20,0:49:52.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so we cared a lot about like kind of a research debt like if you're familiar with this kind of technical debt for programming.\N嗯，所以我们非常关注类似研究债务的问题，就像编程中的技术债务一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:52.08,0:49:57.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh you know like there's a lot of assumptions we made one-off assumptions we made in these papers.\N你知道，我们在这些论文里做了一些临时性的假设。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:57.72,0:49:59.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,It has been pretty consistent.\N一直相当稳定。
Dialogue: 0,0:49:59.32,0:50:04.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh but we really want to show that it is true and there are biases in our like\N但我们真的想证明它是真实的，而且我们的偏好中存在偏见
Dialogue: 0,0:50:04.08,0:50:11.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,in our experiment setup setups different group have different robots and different robot embodiment have different transfer so we\N在我们的实验设置中，不同小组使用不同的机器人，而不同机器人具身形态的迁移能力也各不相同。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:11.44,0:50:17.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,really decided that let's just have the same code base same data set different ways to collect teleprint data\N真正下定决心，就用同一个代码库、同一套数据集，只是用不同的方式来收集电传数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:17.90,0:50:22.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,same way to collect human data and let's see what happens right do we have a consistent finding across\N用同样的方式收集人类数据，看看会发生什么，我们能否在不同情况下得出一致的结论
Dialogue: 0,0:50:22.78,0:50:28.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,different robots um and we found is that it's actually pretty consistent uh so these are kind of\N不同的机器人，我们发现其实相当一致，所以这些算是……
Dialogue: 0,0:50:28.17,0:50:32.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,tiny to see But the uh what we found is very similar to the conclusion of Eagleverse is that\N小到几乎看不见，但我们的发现与EgoVerse的结论非常相似
Dialogue: 0,0:50:32.96,0:50:40.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,aligned data is very very important to uh to in to leverage diverse human data uh the pre-training diverse\N对齐数据对于利用多样化的人类数据进行预训练至关重要。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:40.37,0:50:46.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,human data and uh if you only train on diverse data is not going to give you much gain.\N人类数据，如果你只用多样化数据训练，是很难获得太大提升的。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:46.57,0:50:50.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,So like diverse data plus aligned data is the key to to enable\N因此，多样化数据与对齐数据的结合是关键
Dialogue: 0,0:50:50.75,0:50:57.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,transfer at this scale and we're pretty sure about that across different robots embodiment.\N在不同机器人具身形态下实现这种迁移，我们相当有把握。
Dialogue: 0,0:50:57.60,0:51:03.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and one other thing we did was that we had discovered that uh\N还有件事我们发现了，那就是
Dialogue: 0,0:51:04.00,0:51:09.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,all pre like despite I said that human have a unified embodiment everyone is different.\N尽管我说过人类具有统一的具身形态，但每个人都是不同的。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:09.45,0:51:14.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,We have different body length we have different habit of doing the same task we have different ways to\N我们的身体长度不同，做同一项任务的习惯也不同，方式也各异。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:14.50,0:51:20.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,look at things when have like different habit of like turning our head when I fold shirts and all that.\N观察一下，比如我们叠衣服时转头的习惯，还有其他类似的小动作。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:20.15,0:51:22.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,So a lot of these diversity actually exist in human.\N因此，这些多样性实际上存在于人类之中。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:22.91,0:51:28.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what we found is that if you given the same data budget, if you train on more diverse human data,\N我们发现，如果数据预算相同，训练时使用更多样化的真人数据，
Dialogue: 0,0:51:28.13,0:51:32.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,you actually improve the performance of generalizing to a new human embodiment.\N你实际上提升了模型泛化到新的人形机器人形态的能力。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:32.52,0:51:40.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So there's some consistency to be learned, but you do need diversity in your human data as well to be able to enable uh transfer.\N因此，需要学习一些一致性，但你也需要在人类数据中保持多样性，才能实现迁移。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:40.72,0:51:44.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So and we also visualized this that uh on the left side this is a\N而且我们还进行了可视化，左边这个是
Dialogue: 0,0:51:44.92,0:51:51.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,testing plot of when you train the model with four different demonstrators versus 12 different demonstrators.\N测试了使用四种不同示范者与十二种不同示范者训练模型的效果对比。
Dialogue: 0,0:51:51.11,0:52:00.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you can see that uh this uh this red outlier when you basically we had a hold out demonstrator and we projected back to the test map.\N所以你看，这个红色的离群点，基本上是我们保留了一个演示样本，然后将其投影回测试地图。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:00.14,0:52:06.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,We saw that the outlier is no longer outlier when you have a lot more uh demonstrators.\N我们发现，当你有更多示范者时，这个异常值就不再显得异常了。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:06.30,0:52:12.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,So there it's a lot more mixed in uh when you have when you have more demonstrators.\N所以当演示者更多时，情况就更复杂了。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:12.67,0:52:13.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:13.29,0:52:16.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,So those are I mean there are many other things we did in this study.\N所以，我是说，这项研究中我们还做了很多其他事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:16.30,0:52:17.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you're interested go read the paper.\N如果感兴趣，不妨去读读这篇论文。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:17.84,0:52:18.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's quite fun.\N挺有趣的。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:18.76,0:52:22.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and also you should contribute if you're interested.\N而且如果你有兴趣，也该贡献一份力量。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:22.08,0:52:26.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the consortium is made again made up of a few different labs.\N该联盟再次由几个不同的实验室组成。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:26.39,0:52:36.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so GT is led by my student uh uh Ryan Simmer left two students and Stanford is led\N呃，GTC由我的学生瑞安·西默领导，斯坦福则由两位学生领导。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:36.78,0:52:43.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,by Ze UCSD led by Roger and ETH is led by a whole bunch of students with two PIs.\N由罗杰领导的加州大学圣地亚哥分校团队，以及由一群学生和两名项目负责人领导的苏黎世联邦理工学院团队。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:43.33,0:52:52.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,So this is kind of a our core uh tour core labs and and this couldn't be possible without the support of uh these companies like Meta,\N所以这里是我们核心的参观路线，以及核心实验室，这一切都离不开像 Meta 这些公司的支持。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:52.40,0:52:53.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mecca and Scale.\N麦加与规模。
Dialogue: 0,0:52:53.69,0:53:00.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so uh it's really like a marriage of like academic rigor and we really care about solving problem and they really\N嗯，这就像学术严谨性与我们真正关心解决问题的结合，他们确实很在意。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:00.48,0:53:08.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,care about trying to see what makes their the data they collect useful so I can sell the data to other companies.\N关心的是如何挖掘他们所收集数据的价值，以便我可以将这些数据卖给其他公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:08.13,0:53:14.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,So there there's some synergistic relationship in in this consortium and we're continue to expand.\N因此，这个联盟内部存在一些协同效应，我们正持续扩展。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:14.33,0:53:18.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so we when we release this data set this this thing I got like\N呃，所以我们发布这个数据集时，这东西我感觉就像
Dialogue: 0,0:53:18.42,0:53:25.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,right now it's about 80 or so different entities and individuals who are interested in contributing.\N目前大约有80个不同的机构和个人有兴趣参与。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:25.15,0:53:29.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we're continually growing new new new new uh new companies.\N所以我们一直在不断培育新的、全新的公司。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:29.37,0:53:32.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if you remember I said there's more than 100 companies doing that.\N而且你们要是记得的话，我说过有超过100家公司正在做这件事。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:32.85,0:53:33.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:33.19,0:53:39.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,some of them are interested in really understanding why what makes their data useful.\N其中一些人真正关心的是，弄清楚是什么让他们的数据变得有用。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:39.33,0:53:39.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.\N好的。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:39.92,0:53:40.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, okay.\N嗯，好吧。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:40.47,0:53:42.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, that's that's Eagle Verse.\N所以，这就是鹰verse。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:42.16,0:53:46.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then there's some other open problems I'm curious I'm personally curious about.\N然后还有一些其他开放性问题，我个人很好奇。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:46.42,0:53:50.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,My lab's curious about I'm going to briefly talk about I know we're mostly out of time.\N我们实验室对这个很感兴趣，我简单谈一下，我知道我们时间所剩无几了。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:50.58,0:53:52.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,There are five minutes left.\N还剩五分钟。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:52.74,0:53:59.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, so so uh what I'm interested in essentially is how to better model human essentially.\N呃，我本质上感兴趣的是，如何更好地模拟人类。
Dialogue: 0,0:53:59.10,0:54:06.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh what we are currently facing is that a lot of our designs are model designs are based on assumption\N我们现在面临的问题是，很多设计都是基于假设的模型设计。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:06.12,0:54:14.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,that we are learning from a del demonstr tele demonstration for tabletop task with a highly kind of damped system.\N我们正在从一个桌面任务的演示中学习，这是一个高度阻尼系统的演示。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:14.51,0:54:24.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Basically it's just like if I summarize that like very slow uh moving at creeping speed uh no viewpoint shifts very short like mid horizon task and\N基本上就是我总结一下，就像非常缓慢地移动，几乎像爬行一样，没有视角变化，\N距离很近，就像中等距离的任务一样。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:24.89,0:54:29.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,like I mean we know the how the demonstrator collected data right but when\N就像我们都知道演示系统是如何收集数据的，但当
Dialogue: 0,0:54:29.81,0:54:33.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,you're starting to talk about human data things lot become a lot different so\N你开始谈论人类数据，事情就变得大不一样了。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:33.97,0:54:43.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,what I'm interesting are two parts how do we fully capture the experience of human and how do we model it especially the context of how human\N我感兴趣的是两个方面：如何完整地捕捉人类的体验，以及如何建模这种体验，特别是人类情境下的建模。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:43.18,0:54:48.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,made decisions And my first takes is that first person view is not sensory\N做出了决策，我的第一反应是，第一人称视角并非感官
Dialogue: 0,0:54:48.41,0:54:54.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,experience is not the decision-m context used to actually decide what to do next.\N经验并不是用来实际决定下一步该做什么的决策依据。
Dialogue: 0,0:54:54.48,0:55:01.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh one of the things I'm very curious about is can we measure force or tactile reliably\N还有让我非常好奇的一点是，我们能否可靠地测量力或触觉？
Dialogue: 0,0:55:01.27,0:55:06.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,from human and right now most of developments on the visual side these are nice things that the\N来自人类，而目前视觉方面的大多数进展都是些不错的新鲜玩意儿
Dialogue: 0,0:55:06.80,0:55:13.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,community like the the the the sort of the broader commercial sector have done but the tactile capabilities\N像更广泛的商业领域所做的那样，具备触觉能力
Dialogue: 0,0:55:13.40,0:55:19.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,are quite missing like taco gloves are there but they're not like they're very they're not good yet.\N就像塔可手套一样，虽然有，但还不太行，还没做好。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:19.89,0:55:25.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh there are like other technologies like EMGs to measure like uh muscle activations all that as a\N嗯，还有其他技术，比如肌电图，可以用来测量肌肉激活等各种数据。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:25.76,0:55:30.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,proxy for force or how much force you exert but they are not also very very noisy so\N用来表示力或你施加的力，但它们也相当嘈杂。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:30.65,0:55:37.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,there's a lot of immaturities in the hardware side for really sensorize the entire experience of how you\N硬件方面还有很多不成熟之处，难以真正感知你整个体验的细节。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:37.10,0:55:43.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,kind of how how you perceive the world and the second part is that the context for decision-\N某种程度上，你如何看待这个世界，以及做决策时的背景。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:43.20,0:55:48.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,making is also more than just your instantaneous observation you didn't make your decision about what\N决策不仅仅基于你当下的观察，你做出选择时的考量远不止于此。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:48.50,0:55:52.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,you're going to do next By just looking at the picture you have in front of you,\N你接下来要做的，只是看着你面前的这张图片。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:52.46,0:55:52.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:55:52.73,0:55:54.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have an enormous amount of knowledge.\N你拥有海量的知识。
Dialogue: 0,0:55:54.75,0:55:56.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,For example, this chef, right?\N比如这位厨师，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:55:56.58,0:56:04.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,He like this person cooked because uh well they have taken the class or they have been to a culinary school, right?\N他喜欢这个人做饭，因为嗯，他们上过烹饪课，或者上过厨艺学校，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:56:04.57,0:56:10.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh like it's not because they just look at this like image and they decide oh I'm going to cook.\N而且啊，不是因为他们看了这张图就立刻决定要做饭。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:10.10,0:56:12.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm going to like like turn on the heat, right?\N我要开暖气，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:56:13.02,0:56:21.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,And the person for example turned to different workstations because they remembered that a minute ago they prepared their ingredients in that uh and\N比如那个人想起一分钟前自己在那个工作站准备过食材，于是就转向了那里。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:21.50,0:56:28.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,not on the table and they they had to kind of go back and kind of continue to to to do that kind of thing.\N不在桌上，他们不得不回头继续做这类事情。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:28.22,0:56:35.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So it's it's more than your instantaneous observation and our models right now are terrible at modeling these kind of things.\N所以这不仅仅是你瞬间的观察，而我们现在的模型在建模这类事情上表现得非常糟糕。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:35.28,0:56:44.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so there's a lot of work to be done to be actually be able to what I call behavior clone a human.\N所以要真正实现我所说的行为克隆人类，还有很多工作要做。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:44.16,0:56:51.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,So if you really want to predict behavior of any person what they're going to do next there's a lot of\N所以如果你想真正预测任何人的行为，预测他们下一步会做什么，需要考虑很多因素
Dialogue: 0,0:56:51.56,0:56:57.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,research you need to do and as a first step uh we our lab is doing a lot of different explorations.\N你需要做的研究，作为第一步，我们实验室正在开展各种不同的探索。
Dialogue: 0,0:56:57.28,0:57:01.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,One of the things I'm most excited about is the spatial memory for mobile inflation.\N我最兴奋的一点是移动式膨胀的时空记忆功能。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:01.08,0:57:07.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,So uh it believe it or not we we have the technology to build a lot of these like specially consistent memories right now.\N说实话，你可能不信，我们现在其实已经有技术，可以构建出很多这种特别连贯的记忆了。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:07.81,0:57:11.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,So these are uh one of the ongoing works in our lab that we are building a\N所以这些是我们实验室正在进行的工作之一，我们正在构建一个
Dialogue: 0,0:57:11.61,0:57:18.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,dynamic uh we'll call it dynamic scene graph of object being moved around as you continue demonstrating things.\N动态场景图，随着你不断演示物体的移动而实时变化。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:18.17,0:57:19.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,I've never seen these kind of things before.\N我以前从没见过这种东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:19.90,0:57:25.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you have worked on computer division before uh this is actually a new capabilities I've never seen before.\N如果你之前在计算机部门工作过，那这个其实是全新的功能，我以前从未见过。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:25.09,0:57:33.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh that you can actually track objects and continuously integrate their point cloud on these object to build better object over time.\N也就是说，你可以实际追踪物体，并持续将它们的点云数据整合到这些物体上，\N从而随着时间推移不断优化物体模型。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:33.60,0:57:40.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh and this is all run in real time right so a lot of these foundation models better devices and better\N嗯，这些都实时运行，所以这些基础模型、更优的设备和更好的性能都得以实现。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:40.90,0:57:51.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,like perception models uh are enableing these kind of technology so I'm quite excited about uh this kind of research so takeaways\N就像感知模型正在推动这类技术的发展，所以我对这类研究非常期待，总结一下就是……
Dialogue: 0,0:57:51.32,0:57:59.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh human data is the largest data source of physical intelligence uh human robot transfer is challenging but showing promises uh\N人类数据是物理智能最大的数据来源，人机迁移虽然具有挑战性，但已展现出前景。
Dialogue: 0,0:57:59.54,0:58:09.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,new capabilities merge with model and data scale And data is in fact scaling faster than our scientific understanding of these problems.\N新能力与模型和数据规模相结合，而数据的实际增长速度甚至超过了我们对这些问题的科学理解。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:09.50,0:58:13.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,And scaling science requires really a community effort.\N科学的规模化需要真正的社区协作。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:13.34,0:58:15.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,And with that like to thank you all.\N借此机会，感谢大家。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:15.37,0:58:24.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,And these are the sponsors.\N这些是赞助商。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:24.40,0:58:27.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,A minute.\N一分钟。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:27.92,0:58:28.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:28.34,0:58:35.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the m multimodal that you mentioned at the end is very interesting but as you mentioned it's pretty expensive to collect.\N你最后提到的多模态确实很有趣，但正如你所说，收集起来成本相当高。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:35.45,0:58:41.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I'm just wondering from your experience with the diverse environments would you expect to have like a little bit of this\N所以我想从你在不同环境中的经验来看，你是否会觉得有点类似的情况？
Dialogue: 0,0:58:41.83,0:58:49.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,expensive multimodal data make a big difference so you wouldn't have to collect so much of it to have that's an excellent question.\N昂贵的多模态数据能带来显著差异，因此你无需收集那么多数据就能达到效果，这是一个非常好的问题。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:49.12,0:58:53.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think uh I expect yes I think we could use these uh\N我觉得啊，我预计是的，我觉得我们可以用上这些。
Dialogue: 0,0:58:53.18,0:58:59.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,expensive sensorized human data as supervision to train models to label broader human experience.\N用昂贵的传感人数据作为监督信号，训练模型以标注更广泛的人类经验。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:00.03,0:59:06.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think that should happen but there's there are things that are just inherently not perceivable if you don't have sensors.\N我认为那应该会发生，但如果没有传感器，有些东西本质上是无法感知的。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:06.80,0:59:09.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,For example, imagine that you reach in a bag and start to grab things.\N比如，想象一下你伸手进一个袋子，开始抓东西。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:10.00,0:59:12.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Without tactile, you won't be able to perceive it, right?\N没有触觉，你就无法感知它，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:12.68,0:59:14.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,You can't guess what you're doing.\N你无法猜到自己在做什么。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:14.12,0:59:16.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So these kind of things, not so much.\N这类事情就不太重要了。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:16.72,0:59:23.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,But if you're talking about let's say am I in contact with this cup if I look at from this yes I mean I can perceive this on ego center view.\N但如果说到，比如我是否碰到了这个杯子，如果我从这个角度观察，是的，我的第一人称视角能感知到这个。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:24.01,0:59:31.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Maybe I could use a lab like model train on tactile visual data to label this visually data, right?\N也许我可以像用模型火车那样，用一个实验室来处理触觉视觉数据，对这些视觉数据进行标注，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:31.36,0:59:34.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's definitely possible.\N这绝对是可能的。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:34.64,0:59:35.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah,\N嗯，是的。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:35.44,0:59:43.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,I the same thing as this mountain model and you think about the the neuroscience neuros and also the\N我跟这个山模型是一样的，你想想神经科学、神经元，还有
Dialogue: 0,0:59:43.33,0:59:50.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,the robotics learning reminds me of baby how the baby learn and now your robotics run as a baby,\N机器人学习让我想起婴儿如何学习，现在你们的机器人就像婴儿一样运行。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:50.20,0:59:50.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:50.53,0:59:56.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like baby, you know, how the b how you how the machine learn versus how the baby learn, right?\N就像婴儿一样，你知道的，机器是怎么学习的，和婴儿是怎么学习的，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,0:59:56.96,0:59:57.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm curious to see.\N我很想知道会怎样。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:58.00,0:59:58.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,0:59:58.23,1:00:02.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,Well, the neuroscience side of things is uh is quite interesting because I mean,\N嗯，从神经科学的角度来看，这事儿还挺有意思的，我的意思是，
Dialogue: 0,1:00:02.06,1:00:11.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,if you're talking about like sort of planting sensors in people's brain, uh yes, this this is the most direct form of human data.\N如果你说的是在人脑里植入传感器，嗯，这确实是获取人类数据最直接的方式。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:11.07,1:00:18.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,So maybe we can actually infer more intent from just like like I don't know the more uh more better sensors.\N也许我们仅通过更先进的传感器，就能推断出更多意图。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:18.58,1:00:23.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,But in terms of the way robots learn as human learners, I think right now it's very different.\N但从机器人像人类学习的方式来看，我认为目前差别很大。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:23.57,1:00:28.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh what we're trying to do is the way like it's sort of like large language model analogy.\N我们试图做的，有点像大型语言模型的类比。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:28.26,1:00:34.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,We're not teaching larger language model by teaching how to speak like grammars and everything, right?\N我们并不是通过教语言模型如何像语法一样说话来训练它，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:00:34.14,1:00:37.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,We dump internet.zip into a model, right?\N我们把互联网.zip文件导入模型，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:00:37.68,1:00:44.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,What we're trying to do is to dump human.zip into a model and see what happens, right?\N我们想做的，就是把 human.zip 文件丢进模型里，看看会发生什么，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:00:45.01,1:00:46.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:46.08,1:00:46.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:46.44,1:00:52.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,uh you motivated your talk with uh LSD and how datadriven learning has revolutionized that field.\N嗯，你用迷幻药LSD来激发演讲，还讲了数据驱动学习如何彻底改变了这一领域。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:52.16,1:00:54.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,One thing that's been really important is data quality.\N非常重要的一点是数据质量。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:54.80,1:00:55.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:55.20,1:00:55.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:55.59,1:00:59.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,And uh you often times when we talk about human data can be really noisy.\N而且啊，当我们谈论人类数据时，它往往非常嘈杂。
Dialogue: 0,1:00:59.41,1:01:07.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh what are your thoughts on like filtering out bad data or like how do you do quality control uh etc. Excellent question.\N嗯，关于过滤不良数据或者如何进行质量控制，你有什么看法？非常好的问题。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:07.42,1:01:11.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think that's the next stage of this like once we have more than let's like like\N我认为这就是下一个阶段了，一旦我们拥有的东西超过一定数量，就像这样
Dialogue: 0,1:01:11.65,1:01:15.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,I said we're going to have more data than we know how to do with it right.\N我说过，我们将拥有比我们目前处理能力更多的数据。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:15.16,1:01:23.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,So uh we could yeah we the data filtering understanding like how to explore the data what data attribution right what data matters in\N所以啊，我们可以，嗯，数据过滤和理解，比如如何探索数据，哪些数据属性是关键的，哪些数据才是重要的
Dialogue: 0,1:01:23.52,1:01:32.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,produce that is is the science of pro training is just start starting for for for these kind of models actually wonderful talk really really\N预训练的科学其实就是从这些模型开始的，这是一场非常精彩的演讲，真的非常棒。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:33.04,1:01:36.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,inspiring and interesting work I'm wondering if you can talk a little\N令人振奋又有趣的工作，我想请问您能否谈一谈？
Dialogue: 0,1:01:36.33,1:01:42.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,bit about what you observe after supervised finetuning so what I understood correct\N关于监督微调后你观察到的情况，我理解得对吗
Dialogue: 0,1:01:42.32,1:01:51.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,me if I'm wrong in the middle projects where you were pre-training with large data and then um and then uh testing on specific tasks.\N如果我没理解错的话，在中间的项目中，你们是先用大量数据进行预训练，然后再在特定任务上进行测试。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:51.58,1:01:54.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,You were still pre-training and then mid-train and then supervised fine-tuning.\N你还处于预训练阶段，接着是训练中期，然后是监督微调。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:55.04,1:01:55.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:01:55.84,1:02:00.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do you obtain any degree of generalization after supervised?\N监督学习之后，你能否获得一定程度的泛化能力？
Dialogue: 0,1:02:00.08,1:02:00.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,Great question.\N好问题。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:00.81,1:02:08.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, we we didn't really stress test this but we in the paper but really did a lot of testing.\N是的，我们在论文中并没有真正进行压力测试，但实际上做了大量测试。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:08.28,1:02:12.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,I can't talk too much about this like this is part of the media project um that\N我没法过多谈论这个，因为这属于媒体项目的一部分。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:12.61,1:02:16.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,I can tell you that it does it does have a lot of transfer um from human\N我可以告诉你们，它确实能很好地将人类的经验迁移过来。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:16.70,1:02:22.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,knowledge not in the form of um mostly um so some in the form of spatial analization\N知识并非以某种形式存在，主要是空间分析的形式
Dialogue: 0,1:02:23.04,1:02:29.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,objectization but what's most surprising is the language following became much better I I don't know why like\N对象化，但最令人惊讶的是，后续的语言表达变得好太多了，我也不明白为什么。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:29.72,1:02:34.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,we don't have a good hypothesis of why language following became much better when you pre-tr human\N我们还没有一个很好的假设来解释为什么在预训练人类数据后，语言跟随能力会大幅提升。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:34.19,1:02:41.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,data um but yeah compared with other frontier models like human train human training data is actually most\N数据方面，但说实话，与其他前沿模型相比，人类训练数据实际上是最丰富的。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:41.18,1:02:46.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,effective like we can actually do like for example negative steering like we can actually say don't\N就像我们真的可以做到，比如负向转向，我们真的可以说“不要”。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:46.43,1:02:50.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,do this and actually like try to avoid that object when it when it's trying to do it.\N这样做，实际上要尽量避开那个物体，当它试图这么做时。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:50.67,1:02:50.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:50.96,1:02:54.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Follow up your your human data was also language labelled right.\N后续的人类数据也进行了语言标注，对吧。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:54.64,1:02:59.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh yes yeah yeah that yeah sorry that that that was the reason.\N对，是的，就是那个原因，抱歉，就是那个。
Dialogue: 0,1:02:59.67,1:03:05.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah for other applications there's been a push towards synthetic data to amplify the current existing data.\N其他应用方面，人们正积极推动使用合成数据来扩充现有数据。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:05.29,1:03:11.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Have you also seen that with vision models for robotics or are the general models not there yet?\N你有没有也看到视觉模型在机器人领域的应用？还是说通用模型还没达到那个水平？
Dialogue: 0,1:03:11.36,1:03:13.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh sorry can you rephrase your question?\N抱歉，您能换种方式问一下吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:03:13.60,1:03:18.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh so like synthetic data is really important for other applications like for instance because it's more\N所以，合成数据对于其他应用非常重要，比如因为它更具优势
Dialogue: 0,1:03:18.26,1:03:25.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,reliable but then have you seen people using like generative AI images or videos or just simulation?\N可靠，但你见过有人用生成式AI图像、视频或仿真吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:03:25.20,1:03:27.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Great question.\N好问题。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:27.62,1:03:34.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so the thing is that um the synthetic data is useful because you want something scalable,\N所以，合成数据有用的原因在于，你想要的是可扩展的东西，
Dialogue: 0,1:03:35.04,1:03:45.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,controllable and uh maybe can some characteristics that you want from data that you can manually inject right but for human data right now we can\N可控的，呃，也许你可以手动注入一些想要的数据特征，但目前对于人类数据来说，我们还做不到这一点。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:45.22,1:03:55.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,actually like the way that we for example tell our vendors to is we can have the high degree freedom of control over what behaviors they have.\N实际上，比如我们告诉供应商时，可以对他们行为的控制具有高度的自由度。
Dialogue: 0,1:03:55.60,1:04:01.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,So uh for now I think it's okay to not to only rely on like\N所以呃，目前我觉得没必要只依赖于……
Dialogue: 0,1:04:01.17,1:04:08.38,Sub,,0,0,0,,realistic real world data but uh in the future definitely uh synthetic data will be very\N真实世界的数据，但未来合成数据肯定非常重要
Dialogue: 0,1:04:08.43,1:04:16.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,useful and the one place that where is very very useful is um the last inch\N非常有用，而最实用的地方就是最后一英寸。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:16.16,1:04:22.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,of between your hand and object because human hands are still very different from robot hands,\N因为人手和机器人手之间仍然存在很大差异，
Dialogue: 0,1:04:22.50,1:04:22.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:04:22.89,1:04:30.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then the way that we interact with the object will be subtly but importantly different from how robots should interact with with the object.\N而我们与物体的互动方式，将微妙但重要地不同于机器人与物体的互动方式。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:30.27,1:04:37.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,And this last inch or last newton difference is going to be like we we like basically you want to answer the question if I\N而最后这一英寸或这一牛顿的差距，就好比你要回答这个问题：如果
Dialogue: 0,1:04:37.51,1:04:45.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,were a different person or different robot how I should have done this in order to cause the same effect of this what I have demonstrated.\N如果是另一个人或另一台机器人，我该如何做才能产生与我刚才演示的相同效果。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:45.26,1:04:45.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right?\N对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:04:45.55,1:04:48.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that kind of counterfactual data doesn't exist in the real world.\N这种反事实数据在现实世界中并不存在。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:48.96,1:04:54.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,You have to synthesize it. with language models.\N你必须用语言模型来合成它。
Dialogue: 0,1:04:54.69,1:04:58.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh the big breakthroughs happened first in languages in which a lot of text was\N啊，重大突破最初出现在文本数据丰富的语言中
Dialogue: 0,1:04:58.88,1:05:03.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,already available but then there are also translation models to convert that to other languages.\N已经可以使用，但还有翻译模型可以将其转换为其他语言。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:03.64,1:05:08.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So for parts of the world where neither Ariana or iPhone would be very common.\N因此，在阿丽亚娜或iPhone并不常见的世界部分地区。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:08.16,1:05:11.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do you think that the different kinds of scenes or different ways of doing\N你觉得不同场景或不同做法之间有什么区别吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:05:11.91,1:05:18.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,things could still get some translation benefit from training on these kinds of data sets?\N这些数据集的训练仍可能带来一定的翻译收益吗？
Dialogue: 0,1:05:18.80,1:05:24.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are we talking about like cross the bicep stickers or cross very different kinds of objects maybe\N我们说的是像跨过肱二头肌贴纸，还是跨过完全不同种类的物体？
Dialogue: 0,1:05:24.65,1:05:31.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,or different human preferences of how tasks like how like basically do we need like a everybody\N或者不同人类对如何完成任务的偏好，比如我们到底需不需要每个人都这样
Dialogue: 0,1:05:31.62,1:05:37.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,doing the same task the same way or like diver behavior and diversity right yeah that's a\N用同样的方式做同样的任务，就像鱼类的行为一样，具有多样性和差异性，对吧？是的，就是这样。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:37.14,1:05:41.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,really good question I think um there's this is a I would say there's a paradigm shift\N非常好的问题，我认为这确实标志着一种范式转变。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:42.02,1:05:47.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,how right now as to like how do we design these these models right again like what\N现在关键是怎么设计这些模型，再次强调一下，到底该怎么做？
Dialogue: 0,1:05:47.11,1:05:51.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,I said the VA's A lot of these behavior coding models are designed to fit uni uni\N我说，退伍军人事务部的许多行为编码模型都是为适配单一模型而设计的。
Dialogue: 0,1:05:51.84,1:05:56.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,strategy data and right now you can't really constrain human behavior if if you want to learn\N策略、数据，而目前你根本无法约束人类行为，如果你想学习的话
Dialogue: 0,1:05:57.02,1:06:01.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,from natural human behavior you can't constrain them like that's our goal right so in order to\N从自然的人类行为来看，你无法那样去约束它们，这正是我们的目标，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:06:01.52,1:06:04.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,solve this problem we really need a new type of model to be able to fit this\N要解决这个问题，我们确实需要一种新型模型，才能适配这种复杂情况。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:04.32,1:06:08.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,kind of data and diversity I would say is is the thing it's a problem not a\N数据的种类和多样性才是问题所在，而不是别的。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:08.80,1:06:16.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,solution right we want to solve that to in order to leverage more data yeah similar question\N解决方案，我们想解决这个问题，以便更好地利用更多数据，是的，类似的问题
Dialogue: 0,1:06:16.80,1:06:21.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,um what do you think is the future of Tel operation given all this development and do\N嗯，考虑到这些发展，你认为远程操作的未来会怎样？
Dialogue: 0,1:06:21.46,1:06:27.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,you think how do you think robotic companies will evolve their investment in Telop given how are\N你认为机器人公司会如何调整对TeleOp的投资，考虑到目前的情况？
Dialogue: 0,1:06:27.70,1:06:37.22,Sub,,0,0,0,,you a VC uh because I will give a different answer uh so yeah I think my\N你是风险投资人吗？因为我会给出一个不同的答案，嗯，我觉得我的
Dialogue: 0,1:06:37.27,1:06:43.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,personal goal is to get rid of tail operation because this is just like I said in\N我的个人目标是彻底消除尾部手术，因为正如我所说，这
Dialogue: 0,1:06:43.53,1:06:49.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,the beginning it's a lossy pipe like I I really want my human robots to be humanlike.\N一开始它就像一个有损的管道，我真的很希望我的人形机器人能像人类一样。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:49.98,1:06:57.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,For example, if I throw this water bottle at you, you would either catch it or you flinch, I want my robot to be able to do the same thing.\N比如，如果我朝你扔这个水瓶，你会选择接住它，或者本能地闪躲，我希望我的机器人也能做到同样的反应。
Dialogue: 0,1:06:57.68,1:07:00.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,You would not be able to tell our to demonstrate this repeatedly.\N你根本无法分辨，我们无法反复演示这一点。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:00.77,1:07:03.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is all natural human behaviors, right?\N这些都是自然的人类行为，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:03.39,1:07:04.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want that to happen.\N我希望那能发生。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:04.55,1:07:06.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is my personal goal.\N这是我个人的目标。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:06.72,1:07:12.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:12.64,1:07:13.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, sure.\N哦，当然。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:13.15,1:07:17.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's your opinion on hand important and how much it should match human?\N你认为手部的重要性如何，它应该在多大程度上模仿人类？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:18.00,1:07:20.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Oh, great question.\N哦，好问题。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:20.60,1:07:21.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, yeah.\N嗯，是的。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:21.95,1:07:29.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I mean like I mean I would say yeah like what I said like the last inch gap, right?\N所以，我的意思是，就像我说的，最后那一英寸的差距，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:29.35,1:07:33.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like if you if your hands is very hum like if your robot hands very like there's\N就像如果你的手非常僵硬，就像你的机器人手也一样
Dialogue: 0,1:07:33.32,1:07:37.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,if there's no difference between your robot hands and human hand in terms of kinematics and dynamic capability,\N如果在运动学和动力学能力方面，你的机器人手与人手没有区别，
Dialogue: 0,1:07:37.90,1:07:42.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,you can move really fast, you can move flexibly, you don't need to bridge the gap, right?\N你可以移动得非常快，可以灵活移动，不需要跨越鸿沟，对吧？
Dialogue: 0,1:07:42.30,1:07:44.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's just it just should just work.\N它就应该能正常工作。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:44.66,1:07:48.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so but I mean we're not there yet.\N嗯，但我的意思是，我们还没到那一步。
Dialogue: 0,1:07:48.05,1:07:55.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the like the less humanlike your robot uh hands or factor or the whole body is the\N所以你的机器人手、肢体或整个身体越不像人类，就越……
Dialogue: 0,1:07:55.35,1:08:01.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,more a bigger a gap you have to bridge and the actual transfer that happens will be different.\N你需要跨越的差距越大，实际发生的迁移就会越不同。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:01.28,1:08:02.56,Sub,,0,0,0,,For example,\N例如，
Dialogue: 0,1:08:02.61,1:08:11.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,um like uh like let's say if I have a high higher degree of freedom has than robot than human has then maybe\N比如说，如果我的机器人自由度比人类高，那可能
Dialogue: 0,1:08:11.24,1:08:18.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,the the thing we want to retarget is not the actual kinematic configuration but contact right I want the contact to happen at\N我们想要重新调整的并不是实际的运动学配置，而是接触点，我希望接触能够发生在那里。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:18.42,1:08:25.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,this point in time in in this space like here right and if I have uh ways to exert force similar to how\N此时此刻，在这个空间里，就像这里一样，如果我有类似的方式施加力的话
Dialogue: 0,1:08:25.76,1:08:31.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,human do and can measure force then this is what we should retarget and then the rest of the configuration doesn't really matter Right.\N人类能感知并测量力，所以我们就应该把目标转向这一点，其余的配置其实并不重要，对吧。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:31.92,1:08:33.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,You define a task space.\N你定义一个任务空间。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:33.33,1:08:39.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,The rest you hand over to like a IK or inverse dynamics or learn learn learn solver.\N剩下的部分就交给逆运动学或逆动力学，或者学习、学习、再学习的求解器了。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:39.76,1:08:41.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right.\N对。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:41.76,1:08:42.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:42.09,1:08:50.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the basically the bigger the gap the more work you have to do like to do enable transfer.\N所以，差距越大，你需要做的工作就越多，才能实现迁移。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:50.39,1:08:51.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.\N嗯。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:51.68,1:08:52.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's a lot of great questions.\N问题非常精彩。
Dialogue: 0,1:08:53.02,1:08:57.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thank you.\N谢谢。
